    <p>One last thing worth saying about the Bookstore: it is a level about reading the room rather than about solving anything hard. Both locks are simple once you know what they want — four colour-and-count pairs, four letter values — and everything difficult about it is a matter of misreading an object's role. The poster is a tally sheet. The book with the key on it is a lie. The wall of frames is wallpaper. The teddy bear is a container. The chest is a digit. Once those five sentences are in your head, the level is fifteen minutes of walking, and most of that is the walk between the two rooms.</p>
